00:45:13.420 --> 00:45:14.420
You did.
你们确实打过。

00:45:14.420 --> 00:45:19.500
But also let's be clear when Craig just visited here in Los Angeles 30 years after we used to play that game.
但也要明确一点，就在克雷格30年后访问我们这里的洛杉矶之前，我们曾一起玩过那个游戏。

00:45:19.500 --> 00:45:22.820
He and I and our two friends got together and played Super Bomberman for a while.
他和我和我们的两个朋友聚在一起，玩了一会儿《超级炸弹人》。

00:45:22.820 --> 00:45:23.820
That's right.
没错。

00:45:23.820 --> 00:45:36.340
I was out on LA on a fancy book tour for my debut novel, and then after various book events, I went and played Bomberman with Alec, Joe, and Noah at age 50.
当时我在洛杉矶为我的处女作小说进行一次高级图书巡回宣传，在各种图书活动结束后，我和亚历克、乔以及诺亚在50岁的时候一起去玩了《炸弹人》。

00:45:36.340 --> 00:45:41.380
Just the way Norman Mailer would have.
就像诺曼·梅勒会做的那样。

00:45:41.380 --> 00:45:49.500
So Mick, Mick Giger's perhaps 21 asks, how did you decide on Lily's art style?
那么，Mick Giger（可能 21 岁）问：你们是如何决定莉莉的画风的？

00:45:49.500 --> 00:45:52.519
Like how good or advanced it was or wasn't?
比如它是多么优秀或先进，或者反之？

00:45:52.519 --> 00:45:55.019
And then was it always the same person painting her art?
然后，一直都是同一个人在画她的画吗？

00:45:55.019 --> 00:46:01.320
I was trying to remember this and I realized it's a great question and I'm really upset in my aging brain for not fully memorizing this.
我一直在努力回忆这件事，我意识到这是一个很好的问题，我为我年迈的大脑没有完全记住这一点而感到非常沮丧。

00:46:01.320 --> 00:46:09.699
I think Jenny Hendricks, our writers assistant, along with Matt Coon, wonderful writers assistant who graduated to writing for the show too.
我想珍妮·亨德里克斯，我们的编剧助理，还有马特·库恩——一位出色的编剧助理，后来也晋升为该剧的编剧。

00:46:09.699 --> 00:46:15.579
She would, she did a lot of the art, you practical art you hold that would be held up on camera.
她会，她创作了许多你可以在镜头前展示的实用艺术品。

00:46:15.579 --> 00:46:20.860
I'm pretty sure, I think she did those too, but I can't remember.
我很确定，我想她也做了那些，但我记不清了。

00:46:20.860 --> 00:46:24.980
I will, maybe we can, I'll try to verify this, but I was wondering about it.
我会，也许我们可以，我会试着核实这一点，但我当时就在想这件事。

00:46:24.980 --> 00:46:26.699
I meant to look into it and I didn't care.
我本打算查一下，但我没在意。

00:46:26.699 --> 00:46:30.739
I'm going to text Pam Friman as we talk, made the style for a minute.
我们说话的同时，我要给潘·弗里曼发短信，探讨一下这种风格。

00:46:30.739 --> 00:46:39.260
I kind of like the art is in this weird liminal space between, is that like amateurish or like Matisse?
我有点喜欢这种艺术，它处于一种奇怪的临界空间，这到底是业余的还是像马蒂斯？

00:46:39.260 --> 00:46:40.606
Like, I don't know.
就像，我不知道。

00:46:40.606 --> 00:46:44.219
I can't tell if that's like excellent or not great.
我分不清这到底是极好还是不太好。

00:46:45.820 --> 00:46:48.718
It's yeah, and I'm sure we debated that a little bit.
是的，而且我确信我们对此进行过一些讨论。

00:46:48.718 --> 00:46:52.163
Like, no, she's not supposed to be like a world-class portrait.
比如，不，它不应该像世界级的肖像画。

00:46:52.163 --> 00:46:57.359
She also, one of them is from 20, you know, however many years, not 20 years, 10 years earlier.
而且，其中一幅是来自 20 年前，你知道的，不管多少年前，不是 20 年前，是 10 年前。

00:46:57.359 --> 00:46:59.820
So yeah, I, yeah, I forgot who really did it.
所以，是的，我，是的，我忘了到底是谁画的。

00:47:00.380 --> 00:47:05.820
Well, we have a great letter here and our own Craig Thomas is going to take a read.
嗯，我们这里有一封很棒的信，我们的克雷格·托马斯要来读一下。

00:47:05.820 --> 00:47:08.199
and we'll see if I get an answer.
看看我能不能得到答案。

00:47:08.199 --> 00:47:10.099
This is from Jacob from Nashville.
这是纳什维尔的雅各布发来的。

00:47:10.099 --> 00:47:12.539
Dear Craig, Josh, and Alec.
亲爱的克雷格、乔希和亚历克：

00:47:12.539 --> 00:47:14.059
I've truly been enjoying the podcast.
我真的很喜欢这个播客。

00:47:14.059 --> 00:47:18.500
It's been so much fun to go episode by episode with you through my favorite show of all time.
和你们一起逐集回顾我历来最喜欢的剧集，真是太有趣了。

00:47:18.500 --> 00:47:21.539
In fall 2005, I was a freshman in high school.
2005 年秋天，我是高一新生。

00:47:21.539 --> 00:47:27.500
I convinced my parents that we should watch the pilot during dinner and my John dropped with the Aunt Robin reveal.
我劝说父母在晚饭时看试播集，当鲁本姨妈（罗宾姨妈）揭晓时，我的下巴都惊掉了。

00:47:27.500 --> 00:47:28.619
That's in the pilot, right?
那是试播集里的，对吧？

00:47:28.619 --> 00:47:34.659
The very end of the pilot, armed with a VCR, later a TiVo that could burn DVDs ooh fancy.
试播集的最后，我拿着 VCR，后来又有了能刻录 DVD 的 TiVo——哦，真高级。

00:47:34.659 --> 00:47:37.420
I made sure that my friend group didn't miss an episode.
我确保我的朋友圈不会错过任何一集。

00:47:37.420 --> 00:47:40.820
By the time the show was syndicated on lifetime, we were sitting in many places.
当这部剧在 Lifetime 电视台联合播出时，我们坐在很多地方。

00:47:40.820 --> 00:47:42.940
One of them was lifetime, weirdly.
其中一个地方居然是 Lifetime，真奇怪。

00:47:42.940 --> 00:47:46.099
I had already memorized several of my favorite episodes.
我已经背熟了好几集我最喜欢的剧集。

00:47:46.099 --> 00:47:49.099
Hemium became the shorthand to talk about our lives.
老爸老妈浪漫史成了我们谈论生活的缩写。

00:47:49.099 --> 00:47:52.380
If someone was a little too obsessed with fairness, they were a lily.
如果有人对公平过于执着，他们就是莉莉。

00:47:52.380 --> 00:47:55.980
When I had a crush on someone new, they would try to rein in my tit.
当我迷恋上某个新人的时候，他们会试图控制我的……

00:47:55.980 --> 00:47:58.900
We burned copies of the get psyched mix and had them in our first cars.
我们刻录了“振作起来混音带”，并把它们放在我们的第一辆车里。

00:47:58.900 --> 00:48:09.346
I got a 98% on an essay, my sophomore year of college, how Hymnium was a classic buildings Roman using post-modern storytelling happy to share the final draft please do by the way please send that to us.
我在大学二年级的一篇论文中得了 98 分，论文主题是“《老爸老妈浪漫史》如何是一部采用后现代叙事手法的经典成长小说（Bildungsroman）”，很高兴能分享最终稿——顺便说一句，请务必把那个发给我们。

00:48:09.346 --> 00:48:16.860
The finale aired during the first year of what would eventually be a seven year journey to get my masters and my PhD in speech language pathology.
大结局播出时，正是我攻读言语语言病理学硕士和博士学位的七年漫长征程的第一年。

00:48:17.500 --> 00:48:20.961
I entered the age where the characters start when I needed the most.
我进入了剧中角色开始时的年龄，正是我最需要它的时候。

00:48:20.961 --> 00:48:26.460
I had my first major depressive episode I gained weight I dealt with loss and separation for the first time.
我经历了人生第一次重度抑郁发作，我体重增加，我第一次面对失去和离别。

00:48:27.099 --> 00:48:35.599
Hymnium showed me that all of these things could happen and helped me to handle them with with as much grace as I could, though along the way I felt myself becoming jaded.
《老爸老妈浪漫史》向我展示了所有这些事情都有可能发生，并帮助我尽可能优雅地应对它们，尽管一路上我感到自己变得麻木了。

00:48:35.599 --> 00:48:43.980
In 2020, as I finished my dissertation, I purposely decided to control what I could and live my life out of order.
2020 年，当我完成博士论文时，我刻意决定掌控自己能掌控的事情，以颠倒的顺序过上生活。

00:48:43.980 --> 00:48:47.820
I was ready to be a dad and so I signed up to be a foster parent.
我准备好当爸爸了，所以我报名成为一名寄养父母。

00:48:47.820 --> 00:48:54.380
I finished my dissertation and the foster care classes during lockdown and accepted my first case the day after I defended.
我在封锁期间完成了博士论文和寄养课程，并在答辩后的第二天接受了我的第一个案例。

00:48:54.380 --> 00:49:02.820
Though I experienced more trials with navigating the beginning of my career in foster children, My wonderful son, Jackson, came into my life in June, 2022.
尽管在职业生涯初期和寄养儿童方面遇到了更多的考验，但我出色的儿子杰克逊还是在 2022 年 6 月来到了我的生活。

00:49:02.820 --> 00:49:06.139
His adoption will be finalized around October.
他的收养手续将于 10 月左右最终完成。

00:49:06.139 --> 00:49:11.920
In a very Ted-like roundabout way, that does lead me to my recent reembrace of my inner Ted at 34.
以一种非常“老爸老妈浪漫史”式的兜圈子的方式，这确实引导我在 34 岁时重新拥抱了我内心的泰德。

00:49:11.920 --> 00:49:16.119
When I met my new coworker, Kat, in 2021, she was engaged.
2021 年，当我遇到新同事凯特时，她已经订婚了。

00:49:16.119 --> 00:49:19.599
Eight months after her wedding, Kat Mose beat me.
在她婚礼八个月后，凯特向我表白了。

00:49:19.599 --> 00:49:21.360
She told me that she loved me.
她告诉我她爱我。

00:49:21.360 --> 00:49:25.440
I told her that we had to stop hanging out because it violated the terms of her relationship.
我告诉她我们必须停止交往，因为这违反了她恋爱关系的条款。

00:49:25.440 --> 00:49:27.480
She told me that she and her husband were separating.
她告诉我她和丈夫分居了。

00:49:27.480 --> 00:49:29.414
divorce was final by the end of 2024.
离婚手续于 2024 年底最终完成。

00:49:29.414 --> 00:49:36.211
As I started to listen to the podcast after its premiere and watch the episodes again, all my nascent romanticism came back to me.
当我开始在首播后收听播客并再次观看这些剧集时，我所有初萌的浪漫主义情怀又回到了我身边。

00:49:36.211 --> 00:49:42.277
By the time your matchmaker episode aired, I had asked Kat out on an official date and we've been dating ever since.
在你们的“红娘”那一集播出时，我已经约凯特进行了一次正式的约会，我们从那以后一直约会至今。

00:49:42.277 --> 00:49:48.603
Our friends have commented that it feels like a sitcom ending and I've been quick to point out that it's a hymium ending.
我们的朋友评论说这感觉像是一个情景喜剧的结局，而我很快指出这是一个《老爸老妈浪漫史》式的结局。

00:49:48.603 --> 00:49:51.322
You asked what makes this show resonate with people.
你问是什么让这部剧引起大家的共鸣。

00:49:51.322 --> 00:49:55.348
Ted taught me that I could live my life in a different order from my friends.
泰德教会了我，我可以以和朋友们不同的顺序过我的人生。

00:49:55.348 --> 00:49:58.904
He taught me that I should take the leap, Metaphorically, of course.
他教会了我应该放手一搏，当然，这是比喻意义上的。

00:49:58.904 --> 00:50:05.492
He taught me that I didn't need to be the hero of the story for my family and my chosen family to still love me and accept me.
他教会了我，我不需要成为故事里的英雄，我的家人和我的挚爱亲朋依然会爱我、接纳我。

00:50:05.492 --> 00:50:12.760
In a way, I have this show and this podcast to thank for my beautiful family from the bottom of my very full heart from one Ted to another.
从某种意义上说，从我这个“泰德”到另一个“泰德”，我由衷地感谢这部剧和这个播客带给我美丽的家庭。

00:50:12.760 --> 00:50:14.459
All I can say is thank you.
我能说的一切只有谢谢。

00:50:14.459 --> 00:50:16.599
Talk about a non-linear narrative.
说到非线性叙事。

00:50:17.239 --> 00:50:18.119
Really, I know.
真的，我懂。

00:50:18.119 --> 00:50:19.116
That's fantastic.
那太棒了。

00:50:19.116 --> 00:50:21.578
That's a beautifully non-linear narrative.
那是一个非常美妙的非线性叙事。

00:50:21.578 --> 00:50:30.020
I love him deciding in the moment to live his life out of order and out of sequence and have fun with editing in his own life to fix it in post.
我喜欢他当机立断决定打破顺序过自己的人生，并在现实生活中通过剪辑来弥补。

00:50:30.020 --> 00:50:36.117
You know we always talk about like musicians get to soundtrack people's lives like this is a weird show.
你知道我们总是讨论音乐人如何为人们的生活配乐，这真是一部奇怪的剧。

00:50:36.117 --> 00:50:37.934
It's soundtrack people's lives.
它为人们的生活配乐。

00:50:37.934 --> 00:50:40.280
It's like a sitcom that is a soundtrack.
它就像一首带配乐的情景喜剧。

00:50:40.280 --> 00:50:41.564
Yeah, that's right.
对，没错。

00:50:41.564 --> 00:50:43.120
It's a beautiful thing.
这是一件美好的事。

00:50:43.120 --> 00:50:43.931
It's a gift.
这是一份礼物。

00:50:43.931 --> 00:50:44.946
Best fans ever.
史上最棒的粉丝。

00:50:44.946 --> 00:50:46.772
Thanks for sharing stories.
谢谢你们分享故事。

00:50:46.772 --> 00:50:59.959
If you want to write in a letter or a voice note that maybe we'll play or read on the show, please go to how we made your mother.com hwmym.com and go up to contact and just follow the directions.
如果你想写信或发语音，我们可能会在节目中播放或朗读，请访问 how we made your mother.com hwmym.com，点击联系并按照说明操作。

00:50:59.960 --> 00:51:01.731
It's pretty self-explanatory.
这其实挺一目了然的。

00:51:01.731 --> 00:51:04.540
We were delighted to spend this time with you.
我们很高兴能和你度过这段时光。

00:51:04.540 --> 00:51:05.639
Craig, I love you.
克雷格，我爱你。

00:51:05.639 --> 00:51:06.442
Alec, I love you.
亚历克，我爱你。

00:51:06.442 --> 00:51:07.150
Love you buddy.
爱你，老兄。

00:51:07.150 --> 00:51:10.502
By the way, Pam Fryman texted, pretty sure it was Jennie, but not sure.
顺便说一句，帕姆·弗赖曼发短信来了，我挺确定是珍妮，但也不是百分之百确定。

00:51:10.502 --> 00:51:12.816
We'll find out and we'll host it in the show now.
我们会查清楚的，然后把它放到节目里。

00:51:12.816 --> 00:51:13.430
It's me, boy.
是我，兄弟。

00:51:13.430 --> 00:51:14.280
I'll have amnesia.
我会失忆的。

00:51:14.280 --> 00:51:16.323
This is us all just aging in real time.
这就是我们所有人都在实时变老。

00:51:16.323 --> 00:51:22.978
Well, thanks also to Doug and Alex and Emily and our our whole team over here and and Jenna and Angela and everyone in Odyssey.
嗯，还要感谢道格、亚历克斯、艾米丽以及我们在这里的整个团队，还有珍娜、安吉拉和Audacy的每个人。

00:51:22.978 --> 00:51:24.078
Thanks for tuning in.
感谢收听。

00:51:24.078 --> 00:51:30.208
And if you love this show and you know other how I met your mother and friends who aren't watch is listening somehow.
如果你热爱这部剧，而且你认识其他《老爸老妈浪漫史》的剧迷，他们不知怎么地只听不看。

00:51:30.208 --> 00:51:31.414
We don't watch anymore.
我们不再看了。

00:51:31.414 --> 00:51:32.199
We just listen.
我们只听。

00:51:33.320 --> 00:51:37.294
Please do them a favor and tell them about the show and we'll see you next time.
请帮他们一个忙，把这部剧推荐给他们，我们下期再见。

00:51:37.294 --> 00:51:38.039
Thanks so much.
非常感谢。

00:51:41.389 --> 00:51:44.222
Please equip me all sins off again.
请再次把所有罪过都推到我身上。

